the super-user to run a program as if another user executed it. It is
similar to 'su', but easier to use for routine tasks.

	In addition, it allows the priority of the executed program to be
modified. It also allows standard input, output, and error to be redirected
or closed. The target program can optionally be executed in its own process
group. The program's initial directory can be specified.

